  \RVSPEC & \emph{The RISC-V Instruction Set Manual}, Volume I (Unprivileged ISA) and Volume II (Privileged Architecture); \emph{RISC-V Supervisor Binary Interface Specification}. Free at \url{https://riscv.org/specifications/ratified/} and \url{https://github.com/riscv-non-isa/riscv-sbi-doc}. \\
  \ARMDOC & \emph{Arm Architecture Reference Manual for A-profile architecture} (DDI~0487), and Arm's \emph{Learn the architecture} guides: AArch64 exception model, AArch64 memory management, Generic Timer, GIC. Free at \url{https://developer.arm.com/documentation}. \\
  \SPEC & \emph{Devicetree Specification} (\url{https://www.devicetree.org/specifications/}); \emph{Virtual I/O Device (VIRTIO)}, OASIS (\url{https://docs.oasis-open.org/virtio/virtio/}); the QEMU documentation for the RISC-V and Arm \code{virt} boards (\url{https://www.qemu.org/docs/master/system/}). \\
  \end{tabularx}\par\smallskip
  All four are free. Specifications are revised often, so the reading plans cite them by chapter and section title rather than by page.
